# What this proves, and what it does not:
#
# [V] both handovers are advertised - the descriptor carries
#     kOfxImageEffectPropOpenCLRenderSupported (Buffers) and
#     kOfxImageEffectPropOpenCLSupported (Images) once the host advertises both.
# [V] with an image2d_t in kOfxImageEffectPropOpenCLImage and no cl_mem in
#     kOfxImagePropData, the plug-in takes the image path: the host's seeded
#     destination image changes (the write went through the device, not through
#     the host pointer that is still published), and the frame is the source
#     times two bit for bit.
# [V] the image kernel addresses by coordinates: a 11,3..45,41 window changes
#     only the window, and the pixels outside still hold the previous full-frame
#     result.
# [V] the two programs coexist: switching the host back to the Buffers handover
#     renders again, with the buffer kernel that was already built.
# [V] the plug-in chooses by property, not by mode flag: the host sets only the
#     images property in this pass, which is the rule the header states for a
#     plug-in that supports both handovers.
# [V] the suite leaves nothing behind: stage 8 destroys the instance and unloads
#     the plug-in, so the programs, kernels and factory map are released (the
#     memcheck stage in run-tests.sh, and valgrind-cppcheck.log, hold the numbers:
#     definitely lost 0 bytes).
# [U] every GPU number: PoCL is a CPU device, and this cell has no GPU.
# [U] a device without image support. The suite reports NOT RUN and skips the
#     images stage instead of failing, but only a machine with such a device can
#     show that branch.
